"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I approve PKT-0082. The patch does what the goal asks, and the contract and budget are met. I read the diff only; I did not rerun anything or build sdkjs.\n\n- **Goal:** the cache is now used only when `window[\"NATIVE_EDITOR_ENJINE\"] === true`. Any other value takes the old shaping path, so the browser editor shapes text exactly as before. The new `clearShapeCache()` is exported on `AscCommonExcel` and called from `cell/api.js` when document fonts or a single font finish loading. It only runs on those events, after `StringRender.js` has loaded, so it can't fail on a missing function. The re-measured saving is 13–23 %, the same range as PKT-0077, and the PR text is written.\n- **Contract:** all 2,605 rendered pages are reported identical between the two builds, and the installed `sdk-all.js` was not modified.\n- **Budget:** 4 files and about 106 changed lines, against limits of 6 files and 800 lines.\n- **Record:** the Executor log is filled in, a friction line was added, no follow-up packets were requested, and the surprises are written down: the pinned sdkjs commit `9cea536` is gone so the patch was rebased on `d9e810c`, and the cell build needed 3000 MB of heap.\n\nThings to know before anyone opens the upstream PR:\n- **Smaller cache gap:** the cache key still doesn't record whether the real font file was loaded. That only matters if the cache is later turned on in the browser, where the font-load clearing is meant to cover it.\n- **Cache size:** once the cache holds 200,000 entries it stops adding new ones and never evicts old ones. That keeps memory bounded but loses hits on large files; the PR reviewers should know.\n- **Not tested:** the sdkjs QUnit suites were not run and the browser path was not exercised. The executor reported both openly; they don't block approval.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE native-only gate keeps the browser editor's behavior unchanged, font-load invalidation added, x2t savin